        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Firstly, thank you for all your work on neovim and mini! ❤️\n\n> This was already discussed in [#2338](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2338) with the resolution of \"'mini.ai' will preserve its defaults while documenting a way to remap them\".\n\nAnyway, I'm curious if these keymaps will ever be changed to align with neovim's defaults. As easy as it is [for us to remap mini.ai's](https://github.com/jesseleite/dotfiles/commit/585e5ff5a1f2afffd0ca41ab47d8ad4382f4f1f6), it's kind of a bummer how mini.ai now overrides such a useful core neovim keymap.",
