        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > This was already discussed in [#2338](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2338) with the resolution of \"'mini.ai' will preserve its defaults while documenting a way to remap them\".\n> \n> Anyway, I'm curious if these keymaps will ever be changed to align with neovim's defaults. As easy as it is [for us to remap mini.ai's](https://github.com/jesseleite/dotfiles/commit/585e5ff5a1f2afffd0ca41ab47d8ad4382f4f1f6), it's kind of a bummer how mini.ai now overrides such a useful core neovim keymap.\n\nThe current thinking is that 'mini.ai' suffixes will remain the same, as they are at least as equally useful as the new built-in ones. However:\n- There will be a more thoroughly documented way of having the built-in incremental selection under different keys.\n- In the future there will be a 'mini.ai' module that provides a more flexible incremental selection with its own set of default keys.",
